@startuml
' purpose: the native OpenCode crew, automatic permissions, visible execution and host-auth boundary
' covers: defs/opencode/entrypoint.sh
' covers: defs/opencode/harness.manifest
' covers: defs/opencode/Dockerfile
' covers: defs/opencode/README.md
' covers: defs/opencode/defaults/**
' covers: defs/opencode/sample_opencode.json
' covers: defs/subagents/_frontmatter/opencode/**
' covers: packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh
' covers: packages/lib/proveo-opencode-runtime
' covers: e2e/opencode_auth_test.go
' covers: internal/contract/opencode_presentation_test.go
' covers: e2e/opencode_presentation*
' covers: e2e/testdata/opencode_presentation.*
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title OpenCode crew — automatic asks, explicit denies and visible execution

' Approved native schema and lifecycle: _spec/defs/opencode/native-v2-integration.puml
' Seed order: _spec/packages/lib/seed-and-launch.puml
' Model bridge retirement: _spec/_plans/retire-model-bridging.puml
' Billing and credential decisions: _spec/internal/credentials/credential-decisions.puml
'
' The sibling records implemented source/fixture contracts and PLANNED live acceptance.
' Primary reports persisted offline native TUI and shell-policy fixtures passed.
' Final adversarial/security re-evaluations and latest rebuilt-image/e2e gates remain open.
'
' ── HOW THE GLOBAL CONFIG IS SEEDED WHEN ABSENT ────────────────────────────
' entrypoint seed_defaults delegates to shared proveo_seed; its native bootstrap
' uses baked defaults after config restore and before agent rendering/release.
' It preserves existing JSON, JSONC, and user agent files unless explicitly reseeded.
'
' The old model/small_model env placeholders belonged to the retired bridges.
' An unset placeholder became an empty model persisted in the durable home;
' baked defaults and sample therefore name no default model.
' plan denies edit and shell; build allows edit and retains a shell ask rule.
' The image sets session.permissions: autoaccept through OPENCODE_CLI_CONFIG_CONTENT.
' The runtime separately injects headless run --auto once, regardless of evidence mode.
' Native offline fixtures execute shell ask and preserve explicit deny rejection;
' direct native run without --auto rejects a non-interactive ask.
' Risky-operation house rules remain instructions; they do not create native prompts.
'
' Seeding is MISSING-ONLY unless OPENCODE_RESEED=1, and the same flag re-seeds
' the project AGENTS.md. Everything else the seed writes goes through
' proveo_seed (_spec/packages/lib/seed-and-launch.puml).
'
' ── THE LOCAL MODEL IS A PROVIDER ENTRY, NOT A MODEL STRING ────────────────
' The native writer uses providers.ollama/package/settings and agents.title.model.
' It must register AND select PROVEO_LOCAL_MODEL with one /v1 endpoint suffix.
' Legacy local-model e2e caught an undefined ollama provider falling back to
' a cloud model; a local request must also supply the provider definition.
'
' ── HOST AUTH AND BILLING DECISIONS RETAINED FROM THE ORIGINAL NOTES ───────
' Zen (opencode/<model>) and Go (opencode-go/<model>) use OPENCODE_API_KEY.
' The manifest once omitted env:, leaving forward with nothing to forward,
' the e2e leg skipped, and CredentialReachedAgent unable to name the key.
' An old single-provider auth gate also hid the choice on multi-key hosts.
' subscription: true controls prompting, not a requirement for sandbox login:
' operators may bring another provider key or use an available free model.
' Broker mode holds the real bearer on the host and injects it only for the
' approved gateway route; usable provider keys satisfy launch readiness.
' Historical billing snapshot: Zen had 102 models; Go had 35 models at $10/mo.
' These recorded counts/prices are not a current upstream contract.
' BillingClashes warns, never blocks; Go with Use balance can become metered
' after subscription limits. ModelBilling reads the raw prefix before
' providerAliases folds both routes onto opencode for host/key routing.
' The former auth.json-only explanation described v1, not the v2 token store.
' The approved v2 lifecycle preserves sessions and removes stored credentials;
' the approved private per-run DB and full-lifetime lease live in the native sibling.
' Account/MCP token stores, nonauth state, rebased artifact paths, protected recovery,
' PTY job control and canonical backend mapping now have implemented source fixtures.
' Actual sbx cross-VM file locks and model-driven live idle git sync remain unexecuted.
' Docker remains the sandbox daemon (docker: sbx), not a privileged sibling.
'
' Native CLI config documentation: https://opencode.ai/v2/docs/cli/config
' General editor schema pointer: https://opencode.ai/config.json (v1; advisory).
' Exact session/tabs/mini bindings and schema controls are quoted in the native sibling.
' Presentation semantics and navigation follow primary's native UI/source audit,
' documented in defs/opencode/README.md: source disables Markdown concealment;
' thinking show expands full available returned blocks; high verbosity and grouping
' none expose individual calls and thoughts. Mini tools/thinking/shell_output/
' turn_summary/footer all use show. Tabs use on + status; sidebar uses auto.
' A running subagent row opens the child's live transcript; Ctrl+P -> Toggle subagent
' picker -> Enter provides the alternate route. Opened tabs show busy/attention status.
' No supported default setting renders a live child-operation wait graph in the main
' transcript; Code Mode execute opens a separate Code / Output dialog instead.
' The persisted offline fixture proves eight session/tab Settings values and native
' mini schema controls, not model-driven child operations or live mini output.
' These are upstream native controls, not a custom aligned layout or a new salt surface.
'
' Register: manual normalized word/syllable counts; two sentences per note.
' FK: note right of CREW; words=28 syllables=54; FK 12.6
' FK: note bottom of EP (model); words=30 syllables=56; FK 12.3
' FK: note bottom of EP (auth); words=30 syllables=54; FK 11.5
' FK: note bottom of DEV; words=32 syllables=54; FK 10.6
' FK: note bottom of CLI; words=28 syllables=49; FK 10.5
' FK: note bottom of TRANSCRIPT; words=33 syllables=59; FK 11.9
' FK: note bottom of DISPLAY; words=32 syllables=60; FK 12.8
' FK: note bottom of CHILD; words=30 syllables=52; FK 10.7
'
actor "Developer\nreviews between loops" as DEV

node "opencode container" as CTR <<host>> {
  component "defs/opencode/entrypoint.sh" as EP <<app>>
  component "opencode TUI / run" as CLI <<app>>

  frame "Seeded crew (~/.config/opencode/agents)" as CREW <<host>> {
    component "plan\nread-only: edit + shell denied" as PLAN <<app>>
    component "build\nedit allow · native shell ask rule\nsession.permissions: autoaccept" as BUILD <<app>>
    component "advisors\nedit + shell denied" as REV <<app>>
    component "spec-keeper\nedit allow · shell deny\nedit scope enforced by prompt" as SPEC <<app>>
  }

  component "native LSP\nauto-enabled per detected language" as LSP <<app>>
  artifact "AGENTS.md" as MD <<db>>
  database "/app — repo (rw, .git rw)" as WS <<db>>
  component "defs/opencode/Dockerfile\nOPENCODE_CLI_CONFIG_CONTENT" as DISPLAY <<app>>
  component "opencode session transcript\nmarkdown source · thinking show\ngrouping none · verbosity high\nsidebar auto" as TRANSCRIPT <<app>>
  component "opencode mini\ntools · thinking · shell_output\nturn_summary · footer: show" as MINI <<app>>
  component "opencode subagent rows / picker\nlive child transcripts" as CHILD <<app>>
  component "opencode tabs\nmode on · indicators status" as TABS <<app>>
}

DEV ARROW_MAIN CLI
EP ARROW_MAIN CREW : seed missing only\n(""OPENCODE_RESEED=1"" forces)
EP ARROW_MAIN MD : seed when absent
EP ARROW_MAIN LSP : detect workspace languages
EP ARROW_MAIN CLI : " opencode.json in the durable home \n(no model env; ""--local-model"" writes one) "
CLI ARROW_MAIN BUILD : implement
BUILD ARROW_MAIN WS
CLI ARROW_OPTIONAL PLAN : specs and step lists
BUILD ARROW_QUEUE REV : review loop
BUILD ARROW_QUEUE SPEC : spec maintenance
REV ARROW_MAIN DEV : findings surface to the human
DISPLAY ARROW_MAIN CLI : native CLI preferences; saved global cli.json preserved
CLI ARROW_MAIN TRANSCRIPT : source text + available thinking + individual calls
CLI ARROW_MAIN MINI : five native visibility preferences
CLI ARROW_OPTIONAL CHILD : select running child row / picker
CHILD ARROW_MAIN TABS : opened sessions show status

note right of CREW
  Primary agents separate planning from
  implementation through edit and shell
  permissions. Advisors cannot edit or run shell,
  while spec-keeper retains the existing edit
  exception constrained by its prompt.
end note

note bottom of EP
  The default seed names no model so the harness
  retains model selection. An explicit
  local-model request registers its provider
  and selects that model instead of reviving
  the retired role-to-model bridge.
end note

note bottom of EP
  Host environment keys supply authentication
  without an in-sandbox login step. Broker mode
  keeps the real credential host-side and limits
  gateway injection to approved hosts, while
  the agent holds a sentinel.
end note

note bottom of DEV
  Zen and Go use the same environment key but
  different model prefixes. Billing warnings
  compare the chosen mode with the raw model
  prefix before provider aliases merge both
  routes into one gateway.
end note

note bottom of CLI
  Keep debug logs away from the root TUI because
  log output competes with terminal rendering.
  Headless run can expose logs and thinking blocks
  without corrupting that interactive surface.
end note

note bottom of TRANSCRIPT
  Source Markdown keeps text visible instead of
  concealing it behind a rendered view. Showing
  thinking expands full returned blocks, so
  visibility depends on provider output rather
  than on reasoning the provider never sent.
end note

note bottom of DISPLAY
  High verbosity exposes individual tool calls
  and thoughts instead of reducing the transcript
  to summaries. No grouping keeps each call
  separate, so the operator can attribute
  displayed output to its own operation.
end note

note bottom of CHILD
  Subagent rows and the interactive picker open
  live child transcripts instead of expanding
  every child operation inline. No supported
  default setting draws a live wait graph in
  the main transcript.
end note

note bottom of TABS
  Opened sessions expose busy
  and attention status icons.
end note
@enduml
